A||||14||Loki||TCC bad???? ||||1||
Z||000000||Loki||11-03-2001||11:00 PM||||Having problems with my auto V6 and someone suggested it could be a bad TCC, do to the fact it revs good in park or nuetral but when in gear and i hit the throtle it bogs down and dies......How do I check to see if this is it?????<P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||11-03-2001||11:26 PM||||The way to test the TCC is to unplug it and go for a drive.  If your stalling problems goes away then the TCC was/is bad.  They are a PITA to change, but doable.  <P>I changed the TCC in my 16K mile '88 GT a month or so ago.  It took a few hours, but wasn't that bad.  The hardest part was getting enough fingers in there to plug it in!<P>Unplug it and see what it does.  It is the 4 prong (I think it's blue) plug on the tranny just below the distributor area.<P>Good luck! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||11-04-2001||10:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Loki:<BR><B>could be a bad TCC, do to the fact it revs good in park or nuetral but when in gear and i hit the throtle it bogs down and dies......How do I check to see if this is it?????<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You just described the classic symptoms of the TCC failing.  Some can be repaired, some have to be replaced.  <P>Anyone know which we have - I just spent $160. getting one replaced on a '95 Cavalier (ugh!) that couldn't be repaired.<P>||||reg||9
Z||000003||mrfiero||11-04-2001||03:09 PM||||I have never heard of fixing a bad or failing TCC switch.  I personally would just buy a new one and save any future hassles.  The part is about $50, so if you do it yourself it is a relatively cheap repair.  <P>If you haven't changed your tranny fluid and filter recently, now is a great time.  If you drain the tranny first then you won't lose any fluid when you remove the side panel to access the TCC.  Just a thought.<P>BTW......have you unplugged the TCC?  What's the verdict? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-04-2001||03:15 PM||||The replacement TCC solinoid valves are a revised design to prevent problems.... It's not worth it to fart with an old one that will probably screw up again latter.<P>Replace the third gear pressure switch at the same time. You can get both parts from most autoparts stores or <A HREF="http://www.txchange.com/" TARGET=_blank>Transmission Exchange Co.</A><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnF||11-04-2001||03:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>The replacement TCC solinoid valves are a revised design to prevent problems.... It's not worth it to fart with an old one that will probably screw up again latter.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for the answer to my query!<P>||||reg||7
